**Issue**: #10
Feature: Start Issue
  Start one explicit executable issue on a clean linked branch after proving dependencies.

  Scenario: AC1 current contract
    Given the nmg-sdlc 3.0.0 plugin is installed
    When automated start stage exercises this capability
    Then Given no explicit #N argument, when invoked, then the stage fails closed without a picker or prompt.

  Scenario: AC2 current contract
    Given the nmg-sdlc 3.0.0 plugin is installed
    When automated start stage exercises this capability
    Then Given an issue with unresolved Depends on parents, when starting, then no branch or project mutation occurs.

  Scenario: AC3 current contract
    Given the nmg-sdlc 3.0.0 plugin is installed
    When automated start stage exercises this capability
    Then Given clean state and satisfied dependencies, when starting, then the issue branch is linked and the issue moves to In Progress.

  Scenario: AC4 current contract
    Given the nmg-sdlc 3.0.0 plugin is installed
    When automated start stage exercises this capability
    Then Given leftover unsupported labels, when starting, then they do not create alternate issue types or bypass normal delivery.
